{"id": "2bdc5f79-b14d-48b4-9c07-ad4f32a215f7", "slug": "resilient-logical-frameworks", "title": "Resilient Logical Frameworks", "description": "Resilient Logical Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"Resilient Logical Frameworks\"\ndescription: \"Resilient Logical Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  secondary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  accent: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  background: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  surface: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-primary: \"#111827\"\n  text-secondary: \"#4B5563\"\n  border: \"#E5E7EB\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Resilient Logical Frameworks\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Sourasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 2; favorites: 1; remixes: 0.\nTags: background, animated, webgl, threejs, dither, effect.\n## Overview\nResilient Logical Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nFollow the rendered preview for headline scale, supporting copy, navigation density, and component placement.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #FFFFFF, secondary #FFFFFF, accent #FFFFFF, background #FFFFFF, surface #FFFFFF, text-primary #111827. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Resilient Logical Frameworks</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/matter-js/0.19.0/matter.min.js\"></script>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-slate-900 min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center p-4 sm:p-8 font-['Inter',sans-serif] text-slate-100 overflow-x-hidden\">\n\n    <!-- Main Container -->\n    <div id=\"physics-container\" class=\"relative w-full max-w-6xl aspect-[16/11] sm:aspect-[16/9] bg-slate-950 shadow-sm overflow-hidden flex items-center touch-none select-none\">\n\n        <!-- Subtle Background Grid -->\n        <div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none z-0 opacity-40\"\n             style=\"background-size: 11.11% 16.66%; background-image: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(255,255,255,0.08) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255,255,255,0.08) 1px, transparent 1px);\">\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Geometric Shapes Layer (Physics Bodies) -->\n        <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-10 pointer-events-none\">\n            <!-- Top Left Blue L-Shape -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-blue-600 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 10%; left: 5%; width: 8%; height: 5%;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-blue-600 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 15%; left: 5%; width: 2.5%; height: 16%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Top Purple -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-purple-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 15%; left: 13%; width: 8%; height: 5%;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-purple-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 10%; left: 21%; width: 25%; height: 5%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Top Right Teal -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-teal-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 10%; right: 5%; width: 15%; height: 6%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Mid Teal -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-teal-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 20%; left: 21%; width: 14%; height: 10%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Right Side Accents (Blue, Rose) -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-blue-600 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 19%; right: 5%; width: 8%; height: 2%;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-rose-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 22%; right: 12%; width: 1.5%; height: 2%;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-blue-600 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 28%; right: 11%; width: 9%; height: 3%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Mid Right Blue T-Shape area -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-blue-600 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 32%; right: 20%; width: 15%; height: 4%;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-blue-600 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 36%; right: 20%; width: 6%; height: 12%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Indigo Highlight Block (Behind Text) -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-indigo-600 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"top: 45%; left: 5%; width: 53%; height: 13%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Bottom Right Amber & Purple -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-amber-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"bottom: 24%; right: 11%; width: 9%; height: 11%;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-purple-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"bottom: 10%; right: 5%; width: 6%; height: 5%;\"></div>\n\n            <!-- Bottom Left Amber -->\n            <div class=\"shape absolute bg-amber-500 pointer-events-auto\" style=\"bottom: 10%; left: 5%; width: 15%; height: 2%;\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Typography Content -->\n        <div class=\"relative z-20 w-full pl-[5%] pt-[2%] pr-[5%] pointer-events-none\">\n            <h1 id=\"reveal-text\" class=\"text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight font-light text-white drop-shadow-sm\">\n                <!-- Text populated and masked via JS -->\n            </h1>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Noise Texture Overlay -->\n        <svg class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full z-30 pointer-events-none opacity-[0.15] mix-blend-overlay\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n            <filter id=\"noiseFilter\">\n                <feTurbulence type=\"fractalNoise\" baseFrequency=\"0.8\" numOctaves=\"3\" stitchTiles=\"stitch\"/>\n            </filter>\n            <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" filter=\"url(#noiseFilter)\"/>\n        </svg>\n\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n            gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n            // 1. Setup Masked Word Reveal\n            const textContent = \"Smart systems\\npowered by resilient\\nlogical frameworks.\";\n            const textContainer = document.getElementById('reveal-text');\n            const lines = textContent.split('\\n');\n            let html = '';\n\n            lines.forEach(line => {\n                html += `<div class=\"block\">`;\n                const words = line.split(' ');\n                words.forEach((word, wordIdx) => {\n                    const space = wordIdx < words.length - 1 ? '&nbsp;' : '';\n                    html += `<span class=\"inline-flex overflow-hidden align-top\"><span class=\"reveal-word inline-block translate-y-[110%] pb-2\">${word}</span></span>${space}`;\n                });\n                html += `</div>`;\n            });\n            textContainer.innerHTML = html;\n\n            gsap.to('.reveal-word', {\n                y: '0%',\n                duration: 1.2,\n                stagger: 0.05,\n                ease: \"power4.out\",\n                scrollTrigger: {\n                    trigger: textContainer,\n                    start: \"top 85%\",\n                }\n            });\n\n            // 2. Setup Matter.js Physics integration\n            const { Engine, Render, Runner, Bodies, Composite, MouseConstraint, Mouse } = Matter;\n\n            const engine = Engine.create();\n            const world = engine.world;\n\n            const physicsContainer = document.getElementById('physics-container');\n            const width = physicsContainer.clientWidth;\n            const height = physicsContainer.clientHeight;\n\n            // Boundary Walls\n            const wallOptions = { isStatic: true, render: { visible: false } };\n            const wallThickness = 100;\n            Composite.add(world, [\n                Bodies.rectangle(width / 2, height + (wallThickness / 2), width * 2, wallThickness, wallOptions), // Floor\n                Bodies.rectangle(width / 2, -1000, width * 2, wallThickness, wallOptions), // High Ceiling\n                Bodies.rectangle(0 - (wallThickness / 2), height / 2, wallThickness, height * 3, wallOptions), // Left Wall\n                Bodies.rectangle(width + (wallThickness / 2), height / 2, wallThickness, height * 3, wallOptions) // Right Wall\n            ]);\n\n            // Map DOM elements to Physics Bodies\n            const shapes = document.querySelectorAll('.shape');\n            const shapeBodies = [];\n\n            shapes.forEach((shape) => {\n                const w = shape.offsetWidth;\n                const h = shape.offsetHeight;\n                const x = shape.offsetLeft + (w / 2);\n                const y = shape.offsetTop + (h / 2);\n\n                const body = Bodies.rectangle(x, y, w, h, {\n                    restitution: 0.6,\n                    friction: 0.1,\n                    density: 0.002,\n                    frictionAir: 0.01\n                });\n\n                shapeBodies.push({ body, elem: shape, w, h });\n                Composite.add(world, body);\n\n                // Zero out percentage positions to allow Matter.js absolute translate\n                shape.style.top = '0px';\n                shape.style.left = '0px';\n                shape.style.margin = '0px';\n            });\n\n            // Add Mouse Interaction\n            const mouse = Mouse.create(physicsContainer);\n            const mouseConstraint = MouseConstraint.create(engine, {\n                mouse: mouse,\n                constraint: {\n                    stiffness: 0.2,\n                    render: { visible: false }\n                }\n            });\n            Composite.add(world, mouseConstraint);\n\n            // Keep the mouse in sync with scrolling\n            mouseConstraint.mouse.element.removeEventListener(\"mousewheel\", mouseConstraint.mouse.mousewheel);\n            mouseConstraint.mouse.element.removeEventListener(\"DOMMouseScroll\", mouseConstraint.mouse.mousewheel);\n\n            // Sync Matter.js Body properties to HTML Element transforms\n            Matter.Events.on(engine, 'afterUpdate', () => {\n                shapeBodies.forEach(({ body, elem, w, h }) => {\n                    elem.style.transform = `translate(${body.position.x - w/2}px, ${body.position.y - h/2}px) rotate(${body.angle}rad)`;\n                });\n            });\n\n            // Start Physics Engine\n            const runner = Runner.create();\n            Runner.run(runner, engine);\n\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "resilient-logical-frameworks.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/resilient-logical-frameworks.jpg", "source_name": "resilient-logical-frameworks-DESIGN.md", "views": 57, "forks": 0, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-05-22T07:58:12.433844+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T19:07:44.766317+00:00"}